<LegalLayout title="Terms of Use" updatedAt="July 27, 2026">
  <p>
    Written under Brazilian law: the LGPD (Federal Law No. 13,709/2018,
    Brazil's General Data Protection Law), the Marco Civil da Internet
    (Federal Law No. 12,965/2014, Brazil's Internet Bill of Rights) and the
    Consumer Protection Code (Federal Law No. 8,078/1990). This is the same
    text presented when you sign up in the app — see also our
    <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are and acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    Vayker is an app for organizing group trips: collaborative itineraries,
    shared expense tracking and splitting costs between participants.
  </p>
  <p>
    By creating an account you state that you have read, understood and
    agree to these Terms and to the data handling described in our
    <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you don't agree, please
    don't use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Sign-up and account</h2>
  <p>
    To use Vayker you must be at least 16 years old — users under 18 need
    the consent of a legal guardian, per Article 14 of the LGPD.
  </p>
  <p>
    You're responsible for the accuracy of the information you provide and
    for keeping your credentials safe. Activity on your account is your
    responsibility. Let us know if you notice unauthorized use.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Sharing within trips</h2>
  <p>
    Vayker is collaborative by nature: once you join a trip, your name,
    profile photo and the records you create (itineraries, expenses,
    balances) become visible to the other participants of that trip — and
    only to them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Invitations work by PIN. Only share the PIN with people you want on the
    trip: anyone with the code can join.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Expense splitting is not a financial service</h2>
  <p>
    The amounts, balances and settlement suggestions shown by the app are
    informal records entered by the participants themselves, with no
    banking validation. Vayker does not process payments, does not charge
    fees, and these records do not constitute a debt instrument between
    users.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please review your group's entries: the accuracy of each record is the
    responsibility of whoever created it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use and content</h2>
  <p>
    You retain ownership of the content you submit (photos, text) and grant
    Vayker a limited license to store it and display it to the
    participants of your trips — only as needed to operate the service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Posting unlawful or offensive content, or content belonging to third
    parties without authorization, is prohibited, as is attempting to
    bypass the app's safeguards. Accounts in violation may be suspended or
    terminated.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the service stable, but it's provided "as is" and may
    undergo maintenance and updates.
  </p>
  <p>
    These Terms may be updated; material changes will be communicated in
    the app with reasonable notice. Continued use after they take effect
    counts as agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the Federative Republic of
    Brazil, in particular the LGPD (Federal Law No. 13,709/2018), the
    Marco Civil da Internet (Federal Law No. 12,965/2014) and the Consumer
    Protection Code (Federal Law No. 8,078/1990).
  </p>
  <p>
    The courts of your place of residence have jurisdiction to settle any
    disputes, per Article 101, I, of the Consumer Protection Code.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, requests about personal data, or exercising your LGPD
    rights: reach our data protection contact at
    <a href="mailto:app.vayker@gmail.com">app.vayker@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
